# The build context is the repository root (see src/Pos.Api/Dockerfile), so this
# file decides what the daemon is even shown. Two reasons it matters beyond
# speed: a `bin/` copied from a Windows host poisons the Linux build with stale
# platform-specific output, and anything listed here cannot end up in a layer by
# accident — which is the guarantee wanted for the secret patterns below.

## .NET build output — restored and built inside the image, never copied in
**/bin/
**/obj/
artifacts/
publish/
*.user
*.suo

## Test and coverage output
**/TestResults/
coverage*/
*.trx
*.coverage

## The web app. Built separately and served by its own static host, never by
## the API — a frontend deploy must not restart the backend (Phase 8.1).
src/Pos.Web/

## Test projects and dev-only tools are not part of the API image
tests/
tools/

## Docs, CI and local infrastructure
docs/
.github/
docker/
docker-compose.yml
*.md

## Version control and editor state.
##
## .editorconfig is deliberately NOT here. EnforceCodeStyleInBuild is on and
## warnings are errors, so that file is part of the build contract rather than
## editor cosmetics — it is where CA1861 is turned off for generated migrations.
## Excluding it made the image build apply stricter rules than the host and fail
## on twelve analyzer errors in committed, unmodified migration files.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

## Secrets — nothing matching these may ever reach a layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
appsettings.Development.local.json
appsettings.Local.json
secrets.json
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12

## Local data volumes and OS noise
pgdata/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
